<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">statement has been reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at its meeting held on January 28, 2021.tttttttttttttttttt  nOperating segment information:tttttttttttttttttt  nOn a review of all the relevant aspects including, in particular, the system of internal financial reporting to the Board of Directors, which is the Chief Operating Decision Maker ('CODM'), and considering the economic characteristics of the operations, the Group is of the view that it operates in two segments viz. ‘Engines’ and ‘Lubes’. Lubes segment comprises of a joint venture viz. Valvoline Cummins Private Limited, which is accounted for as per equity method under relevant Ind AS standard. The CODM evaluates the Group's performance based on an analysis of various parameters. Engine segment comprises of Cummins India Limited and other Group Companies which have been aggregated considering the nature of products, class of customer etc. t  nPleases refer quick results for detailed reference.    nttttttttttt  nExceptional items for the quarter and nine months ended December 31, 2019 include expense on account of Voluntary Retirement Program (“VRP”) aggregating to Rs 1,605 Lacs. In addition to VRP,  the exceptional items for the year ended March 31, 2020 include expense on Reduction in Force aggregating to Rs 380 Lacs.  ntttttt  nOther income for the nine months ended December 31, 2020 includes interest on income tax refund amounting to Rs 3,556  lacs. tttttttttttttttttt  nOther expenses for the quarter ended September 30, 2020  and nine months ended December 31, 2020 include an amount of Rs 2,319 lacs pertaining to write off of certain old unusable tangible assets (net book value).tttttttttt  ntttttttttt  nGovernment of India's Code for Social Security 2020 (the 'Code') received assent from the President in September 2020. However, the date from when the Code will become applicable and the Rules have not yet been notified. The Group will assess the impact of the Code and account for the same once the effective date and the rules are notified.ttttttttttttttttttt  nThe Board of Directors of the Company at their meeting held on January 28, 2021 declared an interim dividend of Rs 7 per equity share on 277,200,000 shares of Rs 2 each fully paid-up for the financial year 2020-21.tttttt  nPleases refer quick results for detailed reference.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
